// Title: Potential Persistence Via Excel Add-in - Registry
// Sigma ID: 961e33d1-4f86-4fcf-80ab-930a708b2f82
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2023-01-15 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1137.006
// Description: Detect potential persistence via the creation of an excel add-in (XLL) file to make it run
//   automatically when Excel is started.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/4ae9580a1a8772db87a1b6cdb0d03e5af231e966/atomics/T1137.006/T1137.006.md
//   - https://labs.withsecure.com/publications/add-in-opportunities-for-office-persistence
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_xll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)Software\\Microsoft\\Office.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\Excel\\Options" and RegistryValueData startswith "/R " and RegistryValueData endswith ".xll"
